---
import BaseLayout from "../../../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro";
import MetaPill from "../../../components/ui/MetaPill.astro";
import registry from "../../../data/phase-91-finance-banking-credit-capital-allocation-monetary-systems-financial-stability-registry.json";

const money = registry.money_payments_banking_access_settlement_dossiers;
const credit = registry.credit_underwriting_affordability_servicing_productive_allocation_ledgers;
const capital = registry.capital_markets_institutional_investment_insurance_risk_transfer_registers;
const stability = registry.monetary_policy_systemic_risk_resolution_public_guarantee_democratic_finance_ledgers;
---

<BaseLayout title="Finance, Banking, Credit, Capital Allocation, Monetary Systems And Financial Stability | FTFN" description="Thirty-two inactive money, banking, credit, capital, insurance, monetary-policy, stability, resolution, and democratic-finance records.">
  <section class="page-section hero" data-finance-banking-credit-financial-stability-registry><div class="hero__copy"><div class="eyebrow">FTFN / Financial Systems</div><h1 class="page-title">Account access is not financial inclusion, and financial innovation is not financial stability.</h1><p class="lede">Phase 91 traces money and payment claims; banking access, custody and settlement; credit, affordability, servicing and productive allocation; capital markets, institutional investment and insurance; then monetary policy, systemic risk, resolution, public guarantees and democratic financial governance.</p><div class="meta-row"><MetaPill label="8 inactive money dossiers" tone="possibility" /><MetaPill label="8 inactive credit ledgers" /><MetaPill label="8 inactive capital registers" /><MetaPill label="8 inactive stability ledgers" /><MetaPill label="0 financial-system decisions" tone="review" /></div></div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Money, Payments, Banking Access And Settlement</div><h2>Eight money and banking dossiers remain closed.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/payment-clearing-settlement-custody-continuity-001/">Read the payments and settlement guide</a></div><div class="grid">{money.map((record) => <article class="record-card"><div class="meta-row"><MetaPill label={record.money_state} tone="review" /><MetaPill label="20 inactive gates" /></div><h3><a href={'/evidence/finance-banking-credit-financial-stability/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Monetary claims, issuers, accounts, deposits, wallets, cash, access, fees, identity, privacy, fraud, custody, clearing, settlement, continuity, distribution, review, and receipts remain empty.</p></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Credit, Underwriting, Affordability, Servicing And Productive Allocation</div><h2>Eight credit ledgers contain no eligibility or allocation decision.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/credit-underwriting-pricing-servicing-collections-001/">Read the credit-governance guide</a></div><div class="grid">{credit.map((record) => <article class="record-card"><div class="meta-row"><MetaPill label={record.credit_state} tone="review" /><MetaPill label="20 inactive gates" /></div><h3><a href={'/evidence/finance-banking-credit-financial-stability/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.credit_underwriting_affordability_servicing_productive_allocation_ledger_id}: {record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Borrowers, prices, terms, affordability, models, fairness, servicing, collections, bankruptcy, securitization, additionality, productive use, distribution, and outcomes remain unassessed.</p></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Capital Markets, Institutional Investment, Insurance And Risk Transfer</div><h2>Eight capital and insurance registers remain inactive.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/capital-markets-securities-valuation-liquidity-ownership-001/">Read the capital-markets guide</a></div><div class="source-list">{capital.map((record) => <article class="source-row"><div><h3><a href={'/evidence/finance-banking-credit-financial-stability/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.capital_markets_institutional_investment_insurance_risk_transfer_register_id}: {record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Issuance, ownership, valuation, liquidity, leverage, allocation, stewardship, beneficiaries, insurance, claims, reinsurance, derivatives, public support, stress, distribution, and residual risk remain unassessed.</p></div><MetaPill label={record.capital_state} tone="review" /></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Monetary Policy, Systemic Risk, Resolution, Public Guarantees And Democratic Finance</div><h2>Eight stability ledgers contain no intervention or loss-allocation decision.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/financial-stability-leverage-liquidity-resolution-public-guarantees-001/">Read the financial-stability guide</a></div><div class="grid">{stability.map((record) => <article class="record-card"><h3><a href={'/evidence/finance-banking-credit-financial-stability/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.monetary_policy_systemic_risk_resolution_public_guarantee_democratic_finance_ledger_id}: {record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Mandates, transmission, inflation, employment, housing, systemic importance, leverage, liquidity, stress, supervision, guarantees, recovery, resolution, public control, distribution, emergency authority, normalization, and audit remain inactive.</p><MetaPill label={record.stability_state} tone="review" /></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section briefing-band"><div class="briefing-band__copy"><div class="eyebrow">Public Contract</div><h2>Inspect the empty financial-system state.</h2><p>The export publishes the complete control surface without treating account access as inclusion, credit availability as productive allocation, asset-price growth as durable wealth, capitalization as resilience, central-bank intervention as distributional legitimacy, or innovation as stability—and without admitting, underwriting, allocating, valuing, investing, insuring, intervening, guaranteeing, resolving, scoring, ranking, or changing a stage.</p></div><article class="record-card"><a class="inline-link" href="/data/finance-banking-credit-capital-allocation-monetary-systems-financial-stability.json">Finance, banking, credit, capital, and stability JSON</a></article></section>
</BaseLayout>
